Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:39:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ci: add commit hooks (pre-commit), shared configs, PR
 title check, release preview, dependabot

- Commit hooks with pre-commit, installed once at the root: each tool keeps its own .pre-commit-config.yaml (unchanged, so it keeps working in the old repository), and the root .pre-commit-config.yaml runs them, one hook per tool, through scripts/tool-pre-commit.sh. The script runs a tool's config from inside the tool folder, as in the old repository (pre-commit itself runs hooks from the repository root, where the tools' relative config paths would not resolve), by giving git a view in which the folder is the repository root. Root hooks for the repository-wide files (workflows, dependabot.yml, shared configs) and query-tool's post-merge npm ci. tools/query-tool/.pre-commit-config.yaml: its husky/lint-staged checks and its CI spelling check as hooks.
- shared/ and scripts/sync-shared.py: configs shared by several tools live once in shared/ and are copied into the tool folders listed in shared/files.yaml (commit hook; CI fails on a differing copy). The list starts empty.
- pr-checks.yml: conventional PR titles (action-semantic-pull-request, optional tool scope), an informational release-please dry run in the job summary, and the pre-commit job (all hooks on all files).
- .github/dependabot.yml replaces the per-repo copies; adds grouped Docker base image updates (no major or python minor updates).
- Root pull request template.
